ask(c,'Can I_A=I_C+m[(pᵀp)I3−ppᵀ] directly add tensors expressed in differently oriented axes?', ['No; first express the COM tensor and p in the target orientation','Yes; any two 3×3 tensors can be added without checking bases','Yes; the offset automatically rotates I_C','No; translation can never change an inertia tensor'], ['The source theorem concerns translated parallel frames; components must share one basis.','Matrix size alone does not establish a common physical representation.','The shift correction does not rotate a separately represented tensor.','Translation is exactly what the parallel-axis theorem handles.'],pages=[363,368],difficulty='hard')
